.Dd November 15, 2026
.Dt AUDIOD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm audiod
.Nd RavenBSD audio server and mixer
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
registers the
.Dv audio:
scheme and mixes client PCM streams into the output device.
The first gate serves one null sink,
.Dv audio:out0 ;
it consumes the mixed frames without a hardware driver.
.Pp
A client opens
.Dv audio:out0
and writes interleaved PCM16 through the scheme.
The stream format defaults to 48 kHz stereo; mono and other rates are converted by
.Xr raven-audio-core 3 .
The protocol operations
.Dv SET_FORMAT ,
.Dv START ,
.Dv STOP ,
.Dv DRAIN ,
.Dv SET_VOLUME
and
.Dv GET_STATUS
are described in
.Pa crates/raven-proto-audio/README.md .
.Pp
The null sink mixes one 480-frame period only when every running stream has a full period, so a
cooperative pair of clients never underruns.
.Dv SET_BUFFER
is refused with
.Er ENOTSUP
until the HDA driver path lands.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d/audiod.toml -compact
.It Pa /etc/services.d/audiod.toml
Service manifest.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr play 1 ,
.Xr beep 1 ,
.Xr mixer 1
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
server first appeared in RavenBSD 0.1.
